Fillets: an analytic blend whose contact passes beyond the outline of a
cut-out under an overhanging rim is cut by the faces round the cut-out in
turn, on spines of one edge or several, as one face (mitcad#237, with 0500).

The case: a post whose rim overhangs flats cut into it (the flat's plane
B up to a ledge under the rim, the post's cylinder N going on between the
flats as narrow teeth), the rim rounded where it meets the overhang above.
The contact on N lies below the ledge: over a flat it runs off N into B and
comes back from B at the next tooth. 0055 cuts the blend there by B alone,
but B's plane does not hold the cut over the flat: the blend lies over the
ledge, beyond the flat's outline; the cut runs from where the contact
leaves N up B's plane to the ledge, along the ledge (grown out to the cut)
and down B again. The crossings with the edge between B and the ledge lie
on that edge's prolongations beyond both its ends (0142), just beyond the
gap: the cut on B runs back from where the contact leaves N.

- ChFi3d_KPartCutChain (Round): a chain of faces from B back to B (B, the
  ledge, B), the same edge crossed again further on;
  ChFi3d_KPartEdgeCrossing (BothEnds): the crossing on the prolongation
  beyond either end of an edge whose both ends lie on N, the first along
  the spine. ChFi3d_FillKPartGaps tries such a chain where the cut by B
  alone fails, within the gap widened by the blend's width.
- ChFi3d_KPartChainPieces, ChFi3d_KPartCutPiece (Clamped): pieces kept
  within the gap; where a crossing lies beyond the gap's end, the piece
  between that end and the crossing is of no length along the spine, its
  cut on B its only side (FilDS drops its other side's point-like curve);
  the piece across a closed spine's start is split there (the stripe's
  closing section then is the blend surface's seam). The other contact's
  parameters at the gap's ends are those of the pieces beside it, a period
  on where the line is closed; of the two arcs of a closed line between
  the cut's ends (the ledge's circle), ChFi3d_KPartCutCurve takes the one
  whose change along the spine is the piece's (ExpectedAlong); a point of
  the other contact on a seam gets its tangent and the seam's side the
  piece runs into.
- ChFi3d_FillKPartRoundGapsAcrossEdges: the same across the spine's edges
  (round a closed spine's end too), the pieces split at the edges' ends,
  each on its edge's blend; a piece beside the gap that SplitKPart ends at
  its edge's end with no arc there gets the edge of N it lies on
  (ChFi3d_GiveContactArc).
- PerformSetOfKPart: pieces starting together are ordered with the one of
  no length first; on a closed spine the period starts at a piece starting
  at the spine's start, on a spine of several edges each edge's pieces
  from its start. The torus of an edge between coaxial surfaces of
  revolution (0500), the same as the edge before's, is parametrized as
  that one (ChFi3d_AlignKPartTorus: each edge's torus starts at its edge's
  start), and runs of pieces that are one face (0073) go on across the
  spine's edges (ChFi3d_JoinKPartRunsAcrossEdges), with the faces each
  edge generates.

Upstream: the new paths are taken where the cuts of 0055 and 0071 fail;
the ordering and the period's start change nothing where no piece has no
length or starts at the spine's start.
